                    held-out validation split. We also skip                     
                    any zero‐byte (corrupt) images when                         
                    building our map. This reduces the                          
                    number of parameters being updated and                      
                    the number of epochs, so training                           
                    finishes quickly yet still provides a                       
                    realistic AUROC on held-out data. The                       
                    same script includes a reusable                             
                    `predict()` function for new image                          
                    folders.                                                    
                    Results: The training script ran                            
                    successfully without errors. The model                      
                    was trained for 2 epochs using a                            
                    MobileNetV2 backbone with frozen                            
                    features and a custom classifier head.                      
                    The validation AUROC achieved was                           
                    0.7895, indicating a reasonably good                        
                    ability of the model to differentiate                       
                    between malignant and benign skin                           
                    lesions after limited training.                             
                    Validation Metric: 0.7895                                   
                                                                                
