                    the actual AUROC scores for the folds                       
                    or the mean AUROC, so the exact                             
                    validation metric value is unknown.                         
                    Validation Metric: 0.0                                      
                                                                                
                    -------------------------------                             
                    Design: We can address the long                             
                    training time by using a much lighter                       
                    model and freezing its pretrained                           
                    backbone, training only the final                           
                    classifier for a few epochs on a single                     
                    held-out validation split. We also skip                     
                    any zero‐byte (corrupt) images when                         
                    building our map. This reduces the                          
                    number of parameters being updated and                      
                    the number of epochs, so training                           
                    finishes quickly yet still provides a                       
                    realistic AUROC on held-out data. The                       
                    same script includes a reusable                             
                    `predict()` function for new image                          
                    folders.                                                    
                    Results: The training script ran                            
                    successfully without errors. The model                      
                    was trained for 2 epochs using a                            
                    MobileNetV2 backbone with frozen                            
                    features and a custom classifier head.                      
                    The validation AUROC achieved was                           
                    0.7895, indicating a reasonably good                        
                    ability of the model to differentiate                       
                    between malignant and benign skin                           
                    lesions after limited training.                             
                    Validation Metric: 0.7895                                   
                                                                                
                    -------------------------------                             
                    Design: We propose incorporating data                       
                    augmentation into the training pipeline                     
                    by using RandomResizedCrop, horizontal                      
                    flips, and color jitter to improve                          
                    generalization and reduce overfitting                       
                    when only training the classifier head                      
                    for a few epochs. The validation                            
                    pipeline remains deterministic with                         
                    Resize and CenterCrop. We keep the                          
                    MobileNetV2 backbone frozen and train                       
                    only the final classifier as before,                        
                    printing out the validation AUROC to                        
                    measure the impact of augmentation. The                     
                    predict() function is unchanged aside                       
                    from using the validation transform.                        
                    Results: The training script executed                       
                    successfully without any errors. The                        
                    model was trained for 2 epochs on the                       
                    skin lesion dataset using a MobileNetV2                     
                    backbone with frozen feature layers and                     
                    a custom classifier head. The training                      
                    loss decreased from 0.4120 to 0.3698,                       
                    indicating learning progress. The final                     
                    validation AUROC achieved was 0.7678,                       
                    showing a reasonably good performance                       
                    for differentiating malignant versus                        
                    benign lesions.                                             
                    Validation Metric: 0.7678                                   
                                                                                
                    -------------------------------                             
                    Design: To fix the broadcasting error,                      
                    we need to pool the convolutional                           
                    feature maps into a 1D vector of length                     
                    `backbone.num_features` before                              
                    flattening, instead of directly                             
                    flattening the 4D tensor. We apply the                      
                    model’s `global_pool` to the output of                      
                    `forward_features` and then flatten,                        
                    both in the main feature extraction                         
                    loop and in the `predict` function. We                      
                    also ensure `backbone.feature_dim` is                       
                    set to `backbone.num_features`. Below                       
                    is the corrected script.                                    
                    Results: The training and evaluation                        
                    script ran successfully without any                         
                    errors. The model used a ResNet18                           
                    backbone pretrained on ImageNet to                          
                    extract features, followed by logistic                      
                    regression classifiers trained with                         
                    5-fold stratified cross-validation. The                     
                    mean AUROC across folds was 0.8510 with                     
                    low variance, indicating stable and                         
                    good predictive performance for                             
                    malignancy detection. A submission file                     
                    with predicted probabilities was saved                      
                    correctly.                                                  
                    Validation Metric: 0.851                                    
                                                                                
                    -------------------------------                             
                    Design: I propose to standardize the                        
                    extracted CNN features before training                      
                    the logistic regression classifiers, as                     
                    scaling often improves convergence and                      
                    predictive performance. We will wrap                        
                    the StandardScaler and                                      
                    LogisticRegression in an sklearn                            
                    Pipeline for each fold, fitting the                         
                    scaler only on the training split and                       
                    applying it to the validation split.                        
                    The predict function can remain                             
                    unchanged since each pipeline will                          
                    handle scaling internally. This atomic                      
                    change should yield improved AUROC                          
                    without altering the overall workflow.                      
                    Results: The code executed successfully                     
                    without any errors or bugs. It trained                      
                    a logistic regression model on features                     
                    extracted from skin lesion images using                     
                    a pretrained ResNet18 backbone. The                         
                    model achieved a consistent AUROC score                     
                    around 0.847 across 5 folds, indicating                     
                    a good ability to differentiate                             
                    malignant from benign lesions. A                            
                    submission file with predicted                              
                    probabilities was generated                                 
                    successfully.                                               
                    Validation Metric: 0.8469                                   
                                                                                
                    -------------------------------                             
                    Design: We standardize the extracted                        
                    CNN features before fitting the                             
                    logistic regression by wrapping a                           
                    StandardScaler and LogisticRegression                       
                    into an sklearn Pipeline. This ensures                      
                    that scaling is done per fold correctly                     
                    without leaking information. We retain                      
                    the 5-fold stratified CV, print each                        
                    fold’s AUROC and the mean±std, then                         
                    retrain on all data and output a                            
                    submission.csv in ./working. The                            
                    predict() function remains compatible                       
                    with the pipeline since it uses                             
                    predict_proba.                                              
                    Results: The code executed successfully                     
                    without any errors. The 5-fold                              
                    cross-validation results show a                             
                    consistent AUROC around 0.847,                              
                    indicating the model has good                               
                    discriminative ability between                              
                    malignant and benign lesions. The                           
                    submission file was saved correctly for                     
                    further use.                                                
                    Validation Metric: 0.8469                                   
                                                                                
                    -------------------------------                             
                    Design: I propose replacing the linear                      
                    logistic regression classifiers with a                      
                    small multi‐layer perceptron (MLP)                          
                    wrapped in an sklearn Pipeline together                     
                    with StandardScaler to capture                              
                    non‐linear interactions in the ResNet                       
                    features. We will use a single hidden                       
                    layer of 128 neurons, ReLU activation,                      
                    Adam optimizer, and early stopping to                       
                    prevent overfitting. We’ll perform                          
                    5‐fold stratified CV, printing each                         
                    fold’s AUROC and the mean±std, then                         
                    retrain on all data and generate a                          
                    submission.csv. The existing                                
                    `predict()` function remains compatible                     
                    since MLPClassifier supports                                
                    `predict_proba`.                                            
                    Results: The code executed successfully                     
                    without any errors. The model achieved                      
                    consistent and strong performance                           
                    across the 5-fold cross-validation with                     
                    a mean AUROC of 0.8735 and low standard                     
                    deviation, indicating good                                  
                    generalization. The final predictions                       
                    were saved correctly for downstream                         
                    use.                                                        
